Package: RAssistant
Title: A Lightweight AI Assistant for RStudio
Version: 0.14.0
Authors@R: person("MySimpleSmart", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "120612480+MySimpleSmart@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Opens the existing Source-aware chat assistant in the RStudio
    Viewer. Supports image uploads, optional live console context, contextual R help,
    a project Knowledge Base (PDFs, notes, R examples and custom instructions),
    reviewed Source edits and explicitly approved script validation. Stores optional credentials
    in the operating system credential store, separately from package updates.
License: file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports:
    askpass,
    callr,
    commonmark,
    ellmer (>= 0.5.0),
    htmltools,
    jsonlite,
    keyring (>= 1.3.0),
    knitr,
    later,
    remotes,
    rlang,
    rstudioapi,
    shiny (>= 1.14.0)
Suggests:
    pdftools
URL: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant
BugReports: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant/issues
Config/RAssistant/Changes: Propose fixes as exact Source line ranges, with Copy and Replace for each changed part. Preserve unrelated code, Markdown, chunk fences and options; reject stale, overlapping or out-of-selection proposals.
    Read fresh numbered Source and Markdown/chunk structure. Scan a bounded project file inventory and referenced saved R/Markdown files with Workspace On; include function signatures and relevant in-memory definitions without executing code.
    Isolate the latest captured Console task, retain multiline commands and include datasets referenced there. Keep the newest output when the capture exceeds the request limit. Use the same minimal fixes after approved validation.
